# SQLx/PostgreSQL engineering anchor

Apply when the task touches SQLx, PostgreSQL, repositories, SQL, migrations, persistence, transactions, database concurrency, or query performance.

## Hard invariants

- Data correctness and transactional correctness come before convenience.
- Bind untrusted values; never interpolate external values into SQL syntax.
- Dynamic identifiers/operators come only from trusted typed mappings.
- Universal invariants belong in database constraints where appropriate.
- Transaction scope follows the atomic business operation and remains short.
- Do not hold DB connections/transactions across unrelated slow external calls.
- Avoid unbounded fetches and N+1 query patterns at material scale.
- Concurrency correctness must use PostgreSQL primitives/constraints, not timing assumptions.
- Performance findings require evidence; migrations are production code.

